readable by root alone, and
.Va wireguard_interfaces
in
.Xr rc.conf 5
names it.
.It Cm bird enable | disable | restart | reload Ar protocol
.It Cm bird configure
Tell the BIRD routing daemon through
.Xr birdc 8 ;
.Ar protocol
may be
.Ql all .
.Cm net bird
shows its status, its protocols with what
.Ql show protocols all
says of each, its OSPF neighbours and its tables.
.It Cm bird routes Oo Ar prefix | Cm for Ar address Oc Oo Cm protocol | export Ar name Oc Oo Cm table Ar name Oc Op Cm all
Routes of BIRD's tables, said in the words of
.Xr birdc 8 Ns 's
.Ql show route :
a prefix, or the route that covers an address
.Pq an address alone is taken so ;
those learned from a protocol, or exported to it; those of one table;
with
.Cm all ,
what each carries, a BGP route's path and communities.
They are counted first: more than 2000 are not sent, and the count is
said instead.
.It Cm bird confirm
The configuration put in place with
.Fl s
stays.
.It Cm bird config Op Ar file
Print BIRD's configuration: its main file, or
.Ar file ,
one it includes.
.It Cm bird config Fl w Ar new-text Oo Fl n Oc Op Ar file
Put the text of the local file
.Ar new-text
in its place.
.Xr bird 8
parses the whole configuration first, and what it refuses does not
stay; then the daemon is told to read it.
The file as it was is kept beside it with
.Pa .arcana-old
after its name.
With
.Fl n
it is parsed only.
With
.Fl s
before the command, BIRD is told to take the new configuration back by
itself
.Pq Ql configure timeout
unless
.Cm bird confirm
comes within the time the host allows; the file is then put back as it
was.
.Pp
With the option
.Fl s
before the command, the change is made in safe mode: the host undoes it
unless it hears from the client again within the time it allows.
.Nm
confirms by waiting for the job, so the change stays when the host is
still reachable afterwards, and is undone when the change cut it off.
With
.Fl q
nobody confirms.
Safe mode is for what can be taken back: an address, an interface's
state, MTU and description, an interface made, a route, a jail's
address, a service's variables, and a service started, stopped, enabled
or disabled.
A change that would take away the address the request came in by is
refused unless it is made in safe mode.
.Pp
These run
.Xr ifconfig 8
and
.Xr route 8
on the host as a job, which is waited for unless
.Fl q
only queues it, and change the running system; with
.Fl p
they are kept in
.Xr rc.conf 5
as well: an address as the next
.Va ifconfig_ Ns Ar interface Ns Va _alias Ns Ar n ,
a route under a name of its own in
.Va static_routes ,
an interface made in
.Va cloned_interfaces .
.It Cm agent-build Oo Fl y Oc Oo Fl i Ar key Oc Oo Fl o Ar file Oc Ar repository Op Ar ref
Have the host clone the git
.Ar repository ,
at the branch or tag
.Ar ref
if given, build
.Xr arcana-agent 8
there and send it back.
It is saved as
.Ar file ,
.Pa arcana-agent
by default, after a check against its SHA-256.
For a repository reached over SSH, a host that does not know the
server's host key builds nothing: the fingerprints of the keys the
server showed are printed, with the public key the host shows the
server.
.Fl y
sends those keys back as confirmed, and the host keeps them.
.Fl i
names a private key on the host for git to use instead of the host's
own.
.It Cm console-update Oo Fl y Oc Oo Fl i Ar key Oc Ar repository Op Ar ref
Have the host clone the git
.Ar repository ,
build all of Arcana there, install it over what is installed and
restart the
.Nm arcana_console
service: the console's own update, on the host it runs on.
.Fl y
and
.Fl i
are as for
.Cm agent-build .
.It Cm source-head Oo Fl y Oc Oo Fl i Ar key Oc Ar repository Op Ar ref
The commit at the head of the
.Ar repository Ns 's
branch
.Ar ref ,
or of its default, as
.Nm git ls-remote
on the host tells it: whether there is anything new to build, without
cloning or building.
.Fl y
and
.Fl i
are as for
.Cm agent-build .
.It Cm agent-update Oo Fl r Oc Ar program
Put
.Ar program
in place of the host's
.Xr arcana-agent 8 .
The host checks it against its SHA-256 and by running it with
.Fl V
before it replaces the one installed, which it keeps with the suffix
.Pa .old .
With
.Fl r
the service is restarted; otherwise the new program runs from its next
start.
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl q ,
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop ,
.Cm restart ,
.Cm kill ,
.Cm address ,
.Cm service
actions and variable changes, and
.Cm pkg-upgrade
are queued as a job instead of waited for:
.Nm
prints the job's number and returns.
The host runs its jobs one after another in the order they were queued,
whether or not anyone stays connected, which is what a change that cuts
the connection it was asked over needs.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the request succeeded, 1 when it failed, 2 for usage errors.
